1. PREAMBLE & ETHICAL PURPOSE
This software ("IT Risk & Red Teaming Assessment Engine") is authored exclusively 
for defensive cybersecurity resilience, regulatory compliance validation (including 
DORA Articles 26/27 and TIBER-EU), and authorized, non-destructive IT risk auditing. 
The use of this tooling to assess external surfaces and AI interfaces requires 
uncompromising adherence to explicit legal authorization and ethical standards.

2. GRANT OF PERMITTED USE
Subject to the restrictions set forth herein, the Copyright Holder hereby grants 
authorized users a non-exclusive, revocable license to execute, review, and modify 
this software solely for:
  a) Internal security posture and vulnerability auditing of systems and AI assets 
     strictly owned, operated, or explicitly contracted by the user.
  b) Supervisory and compliance assessments under established testing frameworks 
     (e.g., TIBER-EU, DORA, PTES, NIST SP 800-115).
  c) Academic, educational, and defensive security research conducted within 
     controlled, non-production laboratory environments.

3. STRICT PROHIBITIONS & COMPLIANCE RESTRICTIONS
Any use of this software outside the scope of Section 2 is strictly prohibited. 
You expressly agree and warrant that you shall NOT:
  a) Execute probes, network scans, prompt injections, or testing vectors against 
     any third-party system, IP address, domain, or AI endpoint without prior 
     express, written authorization from the verified legal asset owner.
  b) Utilize this software or any derivative works for unauthorized intrusion, 
     denial of service (DoS), disruption of production services, malware delivery, 
     data exfiltration, or any malicious or unlawful purpose.
  c) Bypass or disable the built-in Scope Boundary Enforcer (ScopeManager), 
     Safety Controller rate limits, or Emergency Stop (Kill Switch) mechanisms 
     when operating outside of isolated offline sandboxes.
  d) Commercialize, relicense, sell, or bundle this software into proprietary 
     commercial SaaS offerings without prior written consent from the Copyright Holder.

4. RULES OF ENGAGEMENT (RoE) MANDATE
All active executions must operate strictly within predefined Rules of Engagement 
defined in an authorization configuration file (e.g., scope.yaml), documenting 
asset ownership, execution windows, rate limits, and SOC deconfliction contacts.

